Committed `29bd06ce8`. At 9.9 base damage, blink behind saved two slices against the closed-plate war machine and one against the turret. The shield robot survived either opening hit. At 19.8, blink behind saved one slice on every target and seed. The shipped 99-damage slice still one-shots all three targets in both arms.

| Slice scale | Target | Median off (s) | Median on (s) | Paired Δ (s) | Faster | Slices off/on |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0.1 | Shield robot | 0.32 | 0.32 | 0.00 | 0/10 | 2/2 |
| 0.1 | War machine, plate closed | 1.03 | 0.32 | −0.72 | 10/10 | 4/2 |
| 0.1 | Sentry turret | 0.32 | 0.02 | −0.30 | 10/10 | 2/1 |
| 0.2 | Shield robot | 0.32 | 0.02 | −0.30 | 10/10 | 2/1 |
| 0.2 | War machine, plate closed | 0.32 | 0.02 | −0.30 | 10/10 | 2/1 |
| 0.2 | Sentry turret | 0.32 | 0.02 | −0.30 | 10/10 | 2/1 |

Five `move_ttk*.gd` probe files now support in-memory slice scaling and re-approach. All 120 timed fights ended in kills at shipped HP. The default-scale run reproduced all 30 archived Kerf pairs. The commit includes the authorized debt baseline update, [report](./evidence/moves/ttk.md), and [per-seed JSON](./evidence/moves/ttk-kerf-whatif.json).

